-- title:
--   Finite map data of exact degree m≥ 2g+1
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring such that every invertible $R$-module is free, let $c\colon C\to\operatorname{Spec}R$ be a proper morphism of schemes which is smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$ (a morphism $\operatorname{Spec}R\to C$ whose composite with $c$ is the identity), and let $\mathcal V$ be a cover of $C$ by two affine opens whose join is $\top$ and whose intersection is again affine. Let $g$ be a natural number with the property that for every algebraically closed field $k$, every morphism $s\colon\operatorname{Spec}k\to\operatorname{Spec}R$, every field extension $L/k$, every `CurveModel` $M$ of $L$ over $k$ (an integral scheme proper and smooth of relative dimension one over $\operatorname{Spec}k$, with $L$ identified with its function field compatibly with $k$, with closed points in bijection with the places of $L/k$ so that stalks correspond to valuation rings, and with every finite set of points contained in an affine open), every isomorphism $e\colon M.C\cong C\times_{\operatorname{Spec}R}\operatorname{Spec}k$ with $e$ followed by the second projection equal to the structure morphism of $M$, every divisor $K_c$ on $L/k$ and every natural number $g'$: if $\ell(D)-\ell(K_c-D)=\deg D+1-g'$ for all divisors $D$ (with $\ell(D)$ the $k$-dimension of the Riemann–Roch space of $D$ and divisors finitely supported integer-valued functions on places), then $g'=g$. Then for every natural number $m$ with $2g+1\le m$ there exists a `FiniteMapData` for $(c,\varepsilon)$ whose degree field equals $m$: affine opens $U,V\subseteq C$ with $U\sqcup V=\top$, with $U$ the complement of the image of $\varepsilon$, sections $f\in\Gamma(C,U)$ and $h\in\Gamma(C,V)$ with $U\cap V=C_f=C_h$ and with the restrictions of $f$ and $h$ to $U\cap V$ mutually inverse, such that $\Gamma(C,U)$ is finite over $R[f]$ and $\Gamma(C,V)$ is finite over $R[h]$ (via the $R$-algebra structures induced by $c$), and such that for every local $R$-algebra $S$ and every $s\in S$ the quotient $S\otimes_R\Gamma(C,U)$ by the ideal generated by $1\otimes f-s\otimes 1$ is a finite free $S$-module of rank $m$.
--
--   This is the existence of a degree-$m$ finite map to the projective line from a relative smooth proper curve with a section, with pole divisor supported on the section, in the classical range $m\ge 2g+1$, packaged as a two-chart datum over a non-local Noetherian base with trivial Picard group. It is used in the construction of the Deligne–Rapoport model package, where [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_finiteMapData_baseChange_away_one_le_m`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_finiteMapData_baseChange_away_one_le_m) invokes it after base change.
